<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
    nexus-wbfpw.48 — make ${svcRole}'s NEW sessions log the plan of every statement, including the
    statements nested inside a function, to the server log.

    WHY: a SECURITY DEFINER function (nexus.text_gate_probe_<dim>, vectors-029) is never inlined, so
    EXPLAIN of a call shows only "Function Scan on text_gate_probe_384" and says nothing about the plan of
    its body. auto_explain with log_nested_statements writes the body's own plan, as ${svcRole} (the role
    the production service connects as, so the owner policy and the row-level-security qual are exactly
    the ones production has), to the server log, which the test reads back through the container's log.

    Per-role and session_preload_libraries, not shared_preload_libraries and not a server-wide minimum
    duration of zero: only sessions opened AFTER this runs, as ${svcRole}, are affected, so a test seeds
    first, runs this, then opens a fresh pool for the measured statements, and neither the migration
    nor the seed floods the log. ALTER ROLE ... SET needs a superuser, hence a changelog the test runs
    on its superuser connection. Run through its own databasechangelog table (see
    PgContainerHelper#enableAutoExplainFor). runAlways, idempotent.
-->
<databaseChangeLog
    xmlns="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog"
    xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
    xsi:schemaLocation="http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog
        http://www.liquibase.org/xml/ns/dbchangelog/dbchangelog-4.4.xsd">

    <changeSet id="test-auto-explain-1" author="nexus-wbfpw.48" runAlways="true">
        <comment>Per-role auto_explain for ${svcRole}: log every statement's plan, nested ones included, with actual rows and timings.</comment>
        <sql splitStatements="false" stripComments="false">
ALTER ROLE ${svcRole} SET session_preload_libraries = 'auto_explain';
ALTER ROLE ${svcRole} SET auto_explain.log_min_duration = '0';
ALTER ROLE ${svcRole} SET auto_explain.log_nested_statements = 'on';
ALTER ROLE ${svcRole} SET auto_explain.log_analyze = 'on';
ALTER ROLE ${svcRole} SET auto_explain.log_format = 'text';
        </sql>
        <rollback>
            <!-- Test-only; the container is thrown away. -->
        </rollback>
    </changeSet>

</databaseChangeLog>
